 ### Opacity Threshold Picking
-A volume picking technique that searches along the viewing ray using the compositing scheme and stops when accumulated opacity exceeds a user-defined threshold, assuming a surface exists at that location [S1]. It is used in VTK, ParaView, MeVisLab, and Voreen (first-hit) [S1]. Pitfalls include: using a zero threshold returns positions in regions surrounding features in "foggy" renderings because every position in the volume has non-zero opacity; using a non-zero threshold may miss relatively transparent but visible regions, causing the ray to reach the end of the dataset and pick the exit position instead of the visible feature [S1].
+A volume picking technique that searches along the viewing ray using the compositing scheme and stops when accumulated opacity exceeds a user-defined threshold, assuming a surface exists at that location [S1]. It is used in VTK and ParaView (opacity threshold), Voreen and Avizo (first-hit), and MeVisLab (opacity threshold or maximum data value) [S1]. Pitfalls include: using a zero threshold returns positions in regions surrounding features in "foggy" renderings because every position in the volume has non-zero opacity; using a non-zero threshold may miss relatively transparent but visible regions, causing the ray to reach the end of the dataset and pick the exit position instead of the visible feature [S1].
 
